---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
---

<PageLayout meta={{ title: "Ultrahuman: Clinical LLM Pipelines — Kiran S Baliga" }}>
	<article class="pt-6 pb-16 sm:pt-8 sm:pb-20">
		<a
			class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-200 mb-8 dark:text-neutral-400"
			href="/#work"
		>
			&larr; Back to selected work
		</a>

		{/* Article Header */}
		<header class="mb-10">
			<span class="block font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400 mb-3">
				Ultrahuman &middot; Engineering case study
			</span>

			<h1 class="font-sans text-[34px] leading-[1.3] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] mb-6">
				Architecting clinical LLM pipelines across 10+ lab stations.
			</h1>

			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300 max-w-2xl">
				At Ultrahuman, I worked in a 3-person health reporting group on the AI clinical reporting pipeline: synthesizing asynchronous multi-station lab diagnostics into 15-page doctor-reviewed health plans, paired with on-device vital computation and global platform localization.
			</p>

			{/* Role & Context Box */}
			<div class="border-y border-[#deded8] my-8 py-5 dark:border-neutral-800">
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-3">
					<div>
						<span class="block font-sans text-sm font-medium text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1]">
							Backend Engineer
						</span>
						<span class="font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400">
							Ultrahuman &middot; Health Reporting Group
						</span>
					</div>
					<div class="sm:text-right">
						<span class="block font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400 tabular-nums">
							Mar&ndash;Jun 2026
						</span>
						<a
							class="font-sans text-sm text-[#262625] hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-200 dark:text-[#f5f4f1]"
							href="https://www.ultrahuman.com"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>
							ultrahuman.com &nearr;
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="font-mono text-xs text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400">
					Ruby on Rails &middot; PostgreSQL &middot; Kotlin Multiplatform &middot; AWS &middot; LLM Orchestration &middot; Prompt Caching
				</p>
			</div>
		</header>

		{/* Context */}
		<section class="space-y-4 mb-12">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[23px] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] mb-3">
				The context
			</h2>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				Ultrahuman builds metabolic and longevity hardware (including the Ring AIR and Blood Vision) trusted by over 5M+ users worldwide. Within a 16-person core engineering team, I worked in a 3-person health reporting group owning the AI report-generation pipeline for performance lab clients.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				Diagnostic blood work, metabolic panels, and physiological markers arrive asynchronously from 10+ independent lab stations over multiple days. Synthesizing these into personalized, doctor-vetted longevity protocols required strict clinical guardrails, idempotent stage processing, and seamless clinician overrides.
			</p>
		</section>

		{/* Ingestion & Clinician Review */}
		<section class="space-y-4 mb-12">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[23px] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] mb-3">
				Asynchronous ingestion DAG &amp; doctor-in-the-loop review
			</h2>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				I built asynchronous background ingestion pipelines that normalize disparate diagnostic data streams into a unified patient graph. Once lab results stabilize, a multi-stage LLM workflow generates personalized recommendations grounded in clinical reference ranges.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				Crucially, high-stakes medical summaries cannot be an unconstrained black box. We implemented a granular section-diffing mechanism: clinicians can reject or modify specific paragraphs, prompting targeted LLM regenerations in under 3 seconds without having to recompute or alter verified sections of the 15-page document.
			</p>

			<div class="border-l-2 border-[#262625] dark:border-[#f5f4f1] pl-5 py-2 my-6">
				<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1]">
					Production reliability in healthcare requires structured ingestion DAGs and surgical section-level regeneration over broad end-to-end prompting.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* On-device KMP Execution & CJK Localization */}
		<section class="space-y-4 mb-12">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[23px] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] mb-3">
				On-device vital computation &amp; modular CJK localization
			</h2>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				Beyond reporting, I ported vital signal processing and SpO&#8322; computation routines from backend Ruby worker queues to Kotlin Multiplatform (KMP). This allowed raw sensor streams to be processed on-device across iOS and Android with 99%+ numerical parity, cutting vital latency by an estimated ~80%.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				To support global expansion, I architected a modular CJK (Chinese, Japanese, Korean) localization system. By injecting verified medical glossaries and leveraging API prompt caching on repetitive context blocks, we reduced translation token costs by ~67% while lifting translation quality evaluation scores from 86% to 91%.
			</p>
		</section>

		{/* What Changed / Metrics */}
		<section class="space-y-6 mb-12">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[23px] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1]">
				What changed
			</h2>

			<div class="space-y-5">
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-6 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-4 dark:border-neutral-800">
					<span class="font-sans text-2xl font-medium text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] w-28 shrink-0">
						86% &rarr; 91%
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[17px] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
						CJK translation quality score improvement with ~67% lower translation token costs via prompt caching.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-6 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-4 dark:border-neutral-800">
					<span class="font-sans text-2xl font-medium text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] w-28 shrink-0">
						~80%
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[17px] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
						Estimated vital calculation latency cut by porting SpO&#8322; algorithms to on-device Kotlin Multiplatform.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-6 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-4 dark:border-neutral-800">
					<span class="font-sans text-2xl font-medium text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] w-28 shrink-0">
						8,000+
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[17px] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
						Powerplug subscription conversions in 60 days via nightly biometric cohort evaluation queues.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* Next Case Study */}
		<div class="border-t border-[#deded8] pt-8 dark:border-neutral-800">
			<div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-2">
				<span class="font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400">Next case study</span>
				<a
					class="font-sans text-[17px] text-[#262625] hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-200 dark:text-[#f5f4f1]"
					href="/work/pencil/"
				>
					Pencil &mdash; AI ad platform infrastructure &rarr;
				</a>
			</div>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300 mt-4">
				Working through a clinical AI or distributed pipeline challenge? <a class="underline hover:text-accent" href="mailto:kiransbaliga@gmail.com">Let’s talk about it.</a>
			</p>
		</div>
	</article>
</PageLayout>
